{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lfo4pki1","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2009 Paper 2 Offline","year":2009,"examDate":2009,"subject":"physics","chapter":"properties-of-matter","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"surface-tension-excess-pressure-and-capillarity","type":"integer","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"ptwo-soap-bubbles-a-and-b-are-kept-in-a-closed-chamber-whe-jee-advanced-physics-motion-bsxvogvmgirbcewy","content":"<p>Two soap bubbles A and B are kept in a closed chamber where the air is maintained at pressure 8 N/m<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.887ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.9 436.6 833.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. The radii of bubbles A and B are 2 cm and 4 cm, respectively. Surface tension of the soap-water used to make bubbles is 0.04 N/m. Find the ratio <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.636ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 2933 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(633,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(12